WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.770
What scene from "The Big Bang Theory" had
Mayim Bialik feeling immensely stressed out

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:06.770
and self-conscious?

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:11.510
Keep watching to find out what happy character
moment felt like a nightmare for the actor.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:16.510
"The Big Bang Theory" was one of television's
longest-running and most successful sitcoms.

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:21.900
Starring Johnny Galecki, Jim Parsons, Kaley
Cuoco, and Mayim Bialik among others, the

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:26.390
show featured a bunch of nerds stumbling through
life and love, trying their best to find their

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:27.919
own personal happiness.

00:00:27.919 --> 00:00:32.820
The show was adored by millions of fans worldwide
during its run, running for an astonishing

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:36.410
12 seasons before finally coming to an end
in 2019.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:41.780
But making the show wasn't without its difficulties
for Bialik, especially when it came to filming

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:44.060
the show's iconic wedding scene.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:49.019
Bialik played the brilliant and Dr. Amy Farrah
Fowler, who meets Dr. Sheldon Cooper, played

00:00:49.019 --> 00:00:51.270
by Parsons, on an arranged date.

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:55.610
She and Sheldon start out a bit rocky, as
tends to be the case with most relationships

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:58.780
Sheldon gets into throughout the show, romantic
or otherwise.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:03.100
But as they get to know one another, their
budding friendship eventually turns into something

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.100
more.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:08.780
She makes him a better man, and once he finally
matures just enough to realize that, he proposes.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:12.500
At the end of Season 11, Amy and Sheldon finally
get married.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:17.210
But while fans of the show were jumping for
joy, behind the scenes, it was extremely difficult

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.620
for Bialik to pretend to be a smiling, happy
bride.

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:25.420
In a blog post published on Grok Nation the
night before the episode aired, she revealed

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:28.130
that it really affected her on a personal
level because,

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:32.630
"As a divorced woman, it's hard to revisit
that moment and those decisions."

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:36.850
She also revealed that prior to filming the
scenes, she had been out sick for a month.

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:40.310
The illness was treated with antibiotics which
promoted weight gain.

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:44.180
She wrote that she, quote, "felt ashamed"
and that she felt like people were judging

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:48.110
her weight and appearance despite the fact
that she had no control over it.

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:49.110
She wrote,

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:52.810
"Even though everyone said I looked beautiful,
I didn't feel completely beautiful."

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:57.100
Feeling down and out regarding her appearance
during her wedding episode of "The Big Bang

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:00.450
Theory" wasn't the only issue Bialik had to
contend with.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:04.420
Like many performers, Bialik has been open
about her battle with anxiety.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:09.500
She spoke about it at length during a 2021
episode of her podcast, "Bialik Breakdown."

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:13.670
While speaking with her "Big Bang Theory"
costar Kevin Sussman, Bialik said,

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:22.730
"With acting stuff, my level of anxiety surrounding
performing is very, very high."

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:26.870
And unfortunately it's only heightened when
she does improvisational acting, something

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:30.100
she was called upon to do occasionally on
"The Big Bang Theory."

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.100
She explained,

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:35.380
"And when I've tried to do things like improv
— things that are very, kind of, free form,

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:36.380
I freeze.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:37.630
I literally freeze.

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:41.630
It's like an instant knot in your throat [...] it's
stuck and there are tears there.

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:42.840
Like, I want to cry."

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:47.510
Many other celebrities, including Ryan Reynolds
and Emma Stone, have also opened up about

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:51.700
dealing with anxiety as individuals who have
to perform for a living.

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:56.620
Even for the most successful stars, it's not
easy, and Bialik went on to discuss how specifically

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.740
it impacted her time on "Big Bang Theory."

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:03.060
"I've had this a handful of times when working
on 'Big Bang Theory' when there was a certain

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:07.120
way they wanted a line delivered, and I was
like, 'Oh okay, I got that.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.660
I'll do that in the next take.'

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.720
And I do it, but it's still not right.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:14.440
And sometimes it's like the audience isn't
laughing, you know it's not funny [...] I

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:19.410
can usually do about four takes or five takes
before my throat starts to do that thing."

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:23.750
While discussing her social anxiety, Bialik
revealed on her YouTube channel that she has

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:26.150
made the decision not to take medication.

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:31.890
"I choose to live with it, and to struggle
through it, and to find new ways that I can

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:34.099
feel freer to be myself."

00:03:34.099 --> 00:03:38.700
Fortunately, there are other ways in which
Bialik manages her anxiety.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:41.940
She revealed that she goes to therapy and
practices meditation.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:44.020
She's also a big fan of weighted blankets.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:49.450
It may have been tough; fortunately, resources
are available to those who struggle with anxiety,

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:53.510
and Bialik was able to do phenomenally during
her time on "The Big Bang Theory."

